1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,380
Actually, Leo's even more upset than you are.

3
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:31,740
Now that I can't compete.

4
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,840
What's the point of Practicing?

5
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:37,190
Sister!

6
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:38,460
I'll cancel it right now!

7
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:40,380
I'll cancel the Sponsorship of
all the Jianghai Team Uniforms.

8
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:41,820
You can't just go back on your word like that.

9
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:44,700
As long as you're willing to keep
contributing to the Jianghai Team,

10
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:45,660
you can also become

11
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:47,100
an Official Reserve Player for the Jianghai Team.

12
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,060
Really?

13
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:54,200
Episode 28

14
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:58,140
Students, inspired by your Coach Tony,

15
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,060
the Tournament Committee has decided

16
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,460
to change the name of this Tournament to:

17
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,860
"The Blazing Teens Yo-Yo Tournament."

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,700
The Team that wins the Championship will be awarded

19
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:11,100
the glorious title of the "Blazing Teens."

20
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,460
And the Individual Champion will be awarded

21
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,860
the glorious title of "Blazing Teen."

22
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,780
Yeah!

23
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:20,430
Blazing Teen!

24
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:21,180
Yeah!

25
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,700
What do you want?

26
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,910
You're the little ant from the Chengnan Team, right?

27
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:00,540
Who are you guys?

28
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:04,380
We on the Chengnan Team always play fair and square.

29
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,260
We don't use dirty tricks.

30
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,660
You don't need to know who we are.

31
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:12,540
If you're from Chengnan, that's enough.

32
00:03:13,180 --> 00:03:14,460
We just wanted to see if the Chengnan Team

33
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:17,340
is really as good as they say.

34
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,740
You want a Match? That's easy.

35
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,620
No need for all this sneaking around.

36
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,500
Cut the crap.

37
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:28,860
If you've got skills, then show them.

38
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:22,000
[Name: Linda] [Team: ???]
[Yo-Yo: Rattlesnake] [Special Move: Double Snake Fission ]

39
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:50,460
Invincible Ice Fissure!

40
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,540
Silver Snake Ice Breaker.

41
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,260
Who the hell are you?

42
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,180
State your names!

43
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,500
Saint Qiao Team's Cold Cat.

44
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,380
Saint Qiao Team's Hot Dog.

45
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:48,540
Just a couple of pets, aren't you?

46
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:34,420
Captain.

47
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,540
We've already engaged them.

48
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:41,340
How'd it go?

49
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,180
They were no match at all.

50
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,020
Should we keep challenging

51
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:51,420
Members of the Jianghai Team and the Chengnan Team.

52
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:55,260
Whatever.

53
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:00,060
Just leave Leo for me.

54
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:29,790
Hey, Student.

55
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,300
Excuse me.

56
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,220
This Tony...

57
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,620
Where's Mr. Tony's Office?

58
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,940
Wow, what a cool gift!

59
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,020
For me?

60
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,860
You sure it's not a mistake?

61
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,100
Wow, what a mysterious gift.

62
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:00,900
Monica, you're still here?

63
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:02,460
Come on, go go.

64
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,340
Coach, let me analyze this for you.

65
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:08,120
This gift is definitely from a woman, right?

66
00:09:08,730 --> 00:09:09,660
Monica!

67
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:11,100
Stop talking nonsense.

68
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,020
Alright, let's go.

69
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,740
Go, go, go.

70
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,020
Hey, Monica.

71
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,340
Don't go blabbing.

72
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,620
Senior Brother, it's me, Dandan.

73
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,540
Your Junior from the the Sports Academy.

74
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:50,940
Do you still remember me?

75
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:53,660
I am going to hold a Birthday Party.

76
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,740
I'm specially inviting you to come.

77
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:57,660
You absolutely must come.

78
00:10:58,600 --> 00:10:59,850
We'll be eagerly waiting.

79
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:06,780
This little brat.

80
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,220
After all these years,

81
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:10,140
she still remembers her Senior Brother.

82
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:17,520
Coach Tony!

83
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,060
Coach Tony, you look so cool!

84
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:26,210
Cool? Could I ever be cooler than you guys?

85
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:29,340
Not "cool." Then it's "Gung su."

86
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,530
Huh, "Gung su."

87
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:33,180
What do you mean "Gung su"?

88
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:35,580
"Gung su" means strong!

89
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,940
Oh, nonsense!

90
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:43,260
You have the perfectly good word "strong,"
and you're reading it as "Gung su."

91
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,660
Is this what they teach you in Chinese class?

92
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:47,100
Coach.

93
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:49,940
But it's internet slang. It's super trendy.

94
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:53,820
It means "Super strong."

95
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,740
Alright, alright, alright, Go on.

96
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:56,700
We're off then.

97
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,140
Bye, Coach Tony.

98
00:12:02,050 --> 00:12:03,030
Coach!

99
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:05,820
Have a great date!

100
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:12,170
Monica, you've got such a big mouth!

101
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:29,340
Senior Brother.

102
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:33,660
Dandan.

103
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:36,540
We've been waiting for you.

104
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:37,980
You've really grown up.

105
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:39,420
I almost didn't recognize you.

106
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:41,340
Do I look that old?

107
00:12:42,180 --> 00:12:43,260
I meant girls change so much as they grow older.

108
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:44,700
You just get prettier and prettier.

109
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:48,030
Tony, since when did you learn

110
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:49,500
to compliment girls?

111
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:52,380
Isn't that what everyone says nowadays?

112
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:53,820
Senior Brother.

113
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:55,260
Oh, Senior Brother.

114
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,140
Do you still recognize me?

115
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:00,540
Of course, of course.

116
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,300
W-William.

117
00:13:03,310 --> 00:13:04,860
Yes, William.

118
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,640
I remember now. Look at my memory.

119
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,220
I remember now.

120
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:13,020
You were in the Class of '90 at our Sports Academy.

121
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:13,980
Exactly, exactly!

122
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,380
Senior Brother, after all these years,

123
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,780
you still look so young.

124
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,700
Oh, come on. I'm getting old.

125
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:23,580
You guys are in the prime of your lives.

126
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:25,500
Senior Brother.

127
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:28,860
We're so thrilled you could make it.

128
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,130
William was worried you'd be too busy with work

129
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:31,740
and couldn't come.

130
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,180
He also told me

131
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:36,060
that today's Birthday Party
absolutely had to have you here.

132
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,460
He's still got so much he wants to say to you.

133
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:39,500
Hold on...

134
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,300
What's this about you two?

135
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:43,260
Senior Brother.

136
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,180
Dandan is my girlfriend now.

137
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:46,620
For real?

138
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,020
That's wonderful, that's wonderful!

139
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:50,940
Ah, I never would've guessed!

140
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:52,860
William.

141
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:55,260
Back at our Sports Academy, you did pretty well.

142
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:59,100
You even won a Silver Medal in the National Sprint.

143
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:01,020
Dandan.

144
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:02,940
As for your results, well,

145
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,380
they're a little embarrassing, aren't they?

146
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:08,220
How could I ever compare to William and you?

147
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:10,620
You were our School's Shotput Champion.

148
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:12,540
How about that?

149
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:15,900
Now I bet you can't even toss a pebble.

150
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:18,000
Dandan!

151
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:20,700
You little brat, still got that sharp tongue.

152
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,620
Senior Brother.

153
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:25,020
Hey, that's just the Sports Academy spirit.

154
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:28,860
Dandan, show the Senior Brother some face.

155
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,870
Sorry about that.

156
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,680
Force of habit.

157
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:33,660
Senior Brother.

158
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:34,970
Shall we take our seats?

159
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:36,540
This way, please.

160
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:37,600
Thank you.

161
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,390
Come, come, Senior Brother.

162
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,380
Please, please.

163
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:05,820
Come on, come on.

164
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:06,780
Everyone.

165
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,220
Let me formally introduce

166
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:12,060
this is my most respected Senior Tony.

167
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,940
He's our Senior Brother from the Sports Academy.

168
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:17,790
Hello, hello, hello.

169
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:18,780
Welcome.

170
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:19,940
Hello, hello.

171
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:23,100
Senior Brother, please sit.

172
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:24,440
Come, this way.

173
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,380
Senior Brother, please sit.

174
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,230
Please have a seat.

175
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:33,150
Everyone, sit, sit, sit.

176
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,090
Come on, come on.

177
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:37,980
Alright everyone.

178
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:40,380
Today is Dandan's birthday.

179
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:42,600
and we have everyone here to celebrate.

180
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:44,700
Lets enjoy ourselves.

181
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,620
Here, let's have a toast.

182
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,990
Here, here.

183
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:49,500
Everyone, be happy.

184
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:49,950
Yeah.

185
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:50,460
Cheers.

186
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:54,300
Who are you?

187
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:55,740
Cold Cat.

188
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:56,700
Hot Dog.

189
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,860
Hmph, you're from the Saint Qiao Team.

190
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:00,510
A pair of pets.

191
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:02,940
I was just looking for you.

192
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:07,260
Hmph, you lost already, and still talking tough?

193
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,660
He's pretty handsome.

194
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:13,020
Wonder if he's just another pretty face with no skill.

195
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:15,420
We'll see who's the one with no skill.

196
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,220
You want to challenge us?

197
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:23,580
You'd better have thick skin, then.

198
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,940
Because you'll lose so badly
your face will be unrecognizable.

199
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,380
Cut the crap.

200
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,300
Is the Cat going first?

201
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:31,740
Or the Dog?

202
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:33,180
Hmph.

203
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:37,020
Soon you won't be so cocky.

204
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:18,000
[Name: Gordon] [Team: Saint Qiao]
[Yo-Yo: Polar Wolf] [Special Move: Wild Wolf Impact ]

205
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:03,420
Tornado Light Wave.

206
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:15,900
Wild Wolf Frenzy.

207
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:36,540
Go back and tell your Chengnan Teammates

208
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:39,900
when you see us two,

209
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,300
keep your distance.

210
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:49,020
Don't ever stand in our way again.

211
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,490
You guys, don't be so cocky.

212
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,200
Senior,

213
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:04,380
Here, let me toast you again.

214
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:05,340
No, no, no.

215
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:06,650
I can't drink anymore.

216
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:07,740
I've already had too much.

217
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:11,100
Today is Dandan's birthday.

218
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:12,540
You have to give us face.

219
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:15,500
Alright.

220
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,820
It's rare you two still remember this Senior Brother.

221
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:19,260
Let's have one more. Cheers.

222
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:21,660
Cheers!

223
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:22,890
Thank you, Senior Brother.

224
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:29,340
Senior Brother.

225
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,260
That one line you said back then...

226
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,660
changed my whole life.

227
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:37,500
I don't have that kind of power.

228
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:39,420
I'm not just saying it.

229
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:43,260
I remember you said that when I won the
Silver Medal in the National Sprint,

230
00:19:43,810 --> 00:19:45,200
I was super proud.

231
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,540
You said, "William..."

232
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,250
"In our Sports Field,"

233
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:56,870
"Silver..."

234
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,810
"is just last place."

235
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:07,260
Being the Champion is our only goal.

236
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:10,140
That's enough, enough, enough.

237
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:20,220
I said something like that?

238
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,140
Of course you did.

239
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:26,940
I remember you only came third in Shotput.

240
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:29,820
Hey, Don't bring up that embarrassing topic.

241
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:31,540
Senior Brother.

242
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:35,100
For your earnest teachings back then,

243
00:20:35,260 --> 00:20:36,060
Let me toast you again.

244
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:38,680
Come.

245
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:48,060
Back then, I was also very young.

246
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:51,420
Full of grand ambitions.

247
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:54,300
Senior Brother, don't say that.

248
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:56,220
Ever since then,

249
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:59,580
I've remembered your words very clearly.

250
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:03,420
"Strive for Excellence in everything, always push forward."

251
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,340
That's why I have a good Career today.

252
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:09,660
Senior Brother, you don't know yet.

253
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:12,060
William is now in the same field as you.

254
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:14,940
He's a PE teacher at Saint Qiao High School.

255
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,860
The benefits are pretty good, too.

256
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:18,730
And his work is well recognised.

257
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:21,540
Really?

